  "title": "RBI Files Review Petition Against Supreme Court's YES Bank AT-1 Bond Write-Off",
  "summary": "The Indian central bank (RBI) sought a review of the Supreme Court's ruling that upheld the Bombay High Court's decision to quash Yes Bank's ₹8,415-crore AT-1 bond write-off, arguing that the administrator lacked the legal authority to proceed. The case highlights ongoing legal battles over financial stability and jurisdiction.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The RBI filed a review petition in the Supreme Court against its judgment that set aside the write-off of ₹8,415 crore of Yes Bank’s additional tier-1 bonds",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court upheld the Bombay High Court's decision to quash the write-off, citing the lack of legal authority for the administrator",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The case is ongoing and involves questions about the legal and financial implications of the bond write-off",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
